  "conditions": "6 AM—Greetings on a fantastic Saturday morning, Jackson. Following yesterday's momentous mountain remodeling, we're moving into the weekend with a renewed exuberance for riding the white wave. The 3 inches that fell while the lifts were spinning yesterday, alongside some helpful overnight wind-work, have created friendly snow surfaces for your springtime sliding pleasure. Puffy morning clouds will give way to deep indigo skies, as high temperatures rise into the mid- to upper 20s at the summit and past the 50-degree mark in Teton Village. A cool northwest breeze in the 5 to 20 mph range will contrast nicely with the warm solar rays landing on your face. So, don't just sit there. The time is now, and the tram is the place! -Lege",
